--
N5008 [meta.unary.prop] is_nothrow_constructible, with [except.spec]/8:
an implicitly-declared or defaulted default constructor is non-throwing
unless the initialization of a subobject (default member initializers,
bases and members' default constructors) is potentially-throwing.  The
built-in __is_nothrow_constructible(T) gave false for mutex_like (a
defaulted default constructor, a default member initializer) and true for
a class whose default constructor is noexcept(false).  libc++'s <mutex>
asserts `is_nothrow_default_constructible<mutex>::value' (mutex.h:47);
the failing static_assert was dropped as a system-header declaration in
about 30 libc++ tests ("dropped 1 system-header declaration").
test_libcxx.desc is that program; it forbids only the mutex.h:47 drop.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept both programs.  The built-in now attempts
`T t;' and walks the implicit/defaulted constructors' subobjects.  Fails
on bin53.
